Section 2 of the Anti-Terrorism Order, in this Order referred to as the principal Order, is amended{a} in the definition of "terrorist", by inserting "directly or indirectly, and wilfully" immediately after "who" in the first line; {b) by inserting the following new definition immediately after the definition of "terrorist entity" - means - {a} any group of terrorists that -

(i) commits, or attempts to commit, terrorist acts by any or indirectly, unlawfully and wilfully;

(ii) participates as an accomplice in terrorists acts (whether or not the terrorist act occurs);

(iii) organises or directs other to commit terrorists acts the terrorist act occurs); or

(iv) abets, contributes, counsels or procures the commission of terrorist acts by a group of persons acting with a where the abetment, contribution, or procurement is made intentionally and with the aim of furthering the terrorist act or with the of the intention of the group to commit a terrorist act (whether or not the terrorist act occurs); or

(b) any class of person declared to be a terrorist group under section 65(1) by the Minister;".

(1) Any person who - (a} provides;

(b) collects;

(c) receives;

(d) possesses; or

(e) makes available, by any means, directly or indirectly, any property, intending, knowing, or having reasonable grounds to suspect, that the property will be used in or in part -

(i) to commit a terrorist act or facilitate the commission of a

(ii) by a terrorist group; or

(iii) by a terrorist, an offence and liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000,000, imprisonment for a term not exceeding 30 years or both.

(2) A person commits an offence under subsection (ll even if (a} a terrorist act does not occur;

(b) the funds will not be used to facilitate, or to engage in, a specific terrorist act; or

(c) the funds will not be used to facilitate, or to engage in, more than one terrorist act.".
